<figure class="chapter-visual boundary-term-diagram">
  <figcaption>
    <strong>原创示意图：分部积分后的体项与边界项</strong>
    <span lang="en">Original diagram: bulk and boundary terms after integration by parts</span>
  </figcaption>

  <svg viewBox="0 0 760 310" role="img" aria-labelledby="boundary-title boundary-desc">
    <title id="boundary-title">Boundary term under fixed and free endpoint variations</title>
    <desc id="boundary-desc">
      A one-dimensional interval contains a bulk Euler-Lagrange term. Fixed endpoint variations make eta vanish at both endpoints. Free endpoints instead require the natural boundary coefficient to vanish.
    </desc>
    <line x1="95" y1="128" x2="665" y2="128" class="boundary-term-diagram__interval" />
    <circle cx="95" cy="128" r="8" class="boundary-term-diagram__endpoint" />
    <circle cx="665" cy="128" r="8" class="boundary-term-diagram__endpoint" />
    <text x="95" y="158" text-anchor="middle">x = 0</text>
    <text x="665" y="158" text-anchor="middle">x = 1</text>
    <text x="380" y="105" text-anchor="middle">bulk: −κ ∫₀¹ n″(x) η(x) dx</text>

    <g transform="translate(50 188)">
      <rect x="0" y="0" width="310" height="88" rx="10" class="boundary-term-diagram__box" />
      <text x="155" y="26" text-anchor="middle">fixed values / Dirichlet admissible variation</text>
      <text x="155" y="51" text-anchor="middle">η(0) = η(1) = 0</text>
      <text x="155" y="74" text-anchor="middle">boundary contribution vanishes</text>
    </g>

    <g transform="translate(400 188)">
      <rect x="0" y="0" width="310" height="88" rx="10" class="boundary-term-diagram__box" />
      <text x="155" y="26" text-anchor="middle">free endpoint variation</text>
      <text x="155" y="51" text-anchor="middle">η is arbitrary on ∂Ω</text>
      <text x="155" y="74" text-anchor="middle">natural condition: κ n′ ν = 0</text>
    </g>

    <text x="380" y="34" text-anchor="middle">δJ = −κ ∫₀¹ n″η dx + κ[n′η]₀¹</text>
    <text x="380" y="62" text-anchor="middle">boundary term = κ(n′(1)η(1) − n′(0)η(0))</text>
  </svg>

  <div class="boundary-term-diagram__fallback">
    <p><strong>固定值边界 | Fixed-value boundary:</strong> 允许的变化满足 <code>η|∂Ω=0</code>，因此边界积分为零。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Fixed-value boundary:</strong> admissible variations satisfy <code>η|∂Ω=0</code>, so the boundary integral vanishes.</p>
    <p><strong>自由边界 | Free boundary:</strong> 变化在边界上任意，驻值条件要求边界系数本身为零，得到自然边界条件。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Free boundary:</strong> the variation is arbitrary at the boundary, so stationarity requires the boundary coefficient itself to vanish, giving a natural boundary condition.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="chapter-visual__contract">
    <p><strong>模型：</strong><code>J[n]=(κ/2)∫₀¹(n′)²dx</code>，<code>κ&gt;0</code>，<code>n</code> 和允许的变化 <code>η</code> 具有完成分部积分所需的正则性。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Model:</strong> <code>J[n]=(κ/2)∫₀¹(n′)²dx</code> with <code>κ&gt;0</code>; <code>n</code> and the admissible variation <code>η</code> have the regularity needed for integration by parts.</p>
    <p><strong>验收：</strong>固定端点时边界项严格为零；自由端点时不能删除边界项，而应读取自然边界条件。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Acceptance:</strong> fixed endpoints make the boundary term exactly zero; with free endpoints it cannot be discarded and instead yields the natural boundary condition.</p>
    <p><strong>边界：</strong>图示是一维标量例子。多维情形的边界项为曲面积分，并含外法向量 <code>ν</code>。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Boundary:</strong> this is a one-dimensional scalar example. In several dimensions the boundary term is a surface integral containing the outward normal <code>ν</code>.</p>
  </div>
</figure>

